WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.111 --> 00:00:01.430
(pensive music)

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:02.740
- [Narrator] Tech companies do way more

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.180
than tech these days.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:07.380
They're now an indispensable
part of our everyday lives

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.530
from how we communicate,

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.880
to how we shop and pay for things.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.510
Many have grown quickly
in less than two decades

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.550
and that's especially true in China.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.520
- Alibaba is the biggest
e-commerce company in the country

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.720
by most measures and runs
a system called Alipay,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.350
which is this phenomenally
important payments platform.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:28.650
- [Narrator] Last year,
more than 700 million people

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.258
used Alibaba's platforms
to buy things online.

00:00:31.258 --> 00:00:33.070
And more than a billion people used

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.230
the FinTech giant Ant Group's mobile app

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.960
to make payments, borrow money,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.700
buy insurance and invest.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:41.030
- We just press Buy.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:42.100
- [Narrator] Alibaba was founded

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.220
by Chinese entrepreneur Jack Ma

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.330
and he's Ant's controlling shareholder.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.043
The two companies helped steer the company

00:00:48.043 --> 00:00:49.960
into the digital marketplace

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.832
and pushed it to become an
increasingly cashless society.

00:00:52.832 --> 00:00:53.870
(scanner beeping)

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.400
Their impact on the economy
has drawn the attention

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.810
of Chinese regulators,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.660
who like their counterparts in the US,

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.500
have been trying to rein in big tech.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.430
- There isn't much really that governments

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.280
in Washington and in
Beijing can all agree on

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.480
but at the moment, a push is underway

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.090
to curb the power of the
world's biggest tech giants.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.440
China appears to be moving

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:16.810
on a faster timeframe for
much of this than the US.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.880
- [Narrator] Here's how China was able

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.680
to bring Jack Ma's companies in line

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.913
in just a few months.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.330
The main driver of why China can move fast

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:26.330
is because of it's political system.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:29.810
- China is a highly
centralized, one-party state

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:31.710
and so that means in turn

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.640
that when the Chinese
authorities do decide

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.240
to do something, they can
sometimes move much faster.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:39.280
- [Narrator] and that type of speed

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:41.230
when it comes to regulatory action

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:44.647
was on full display with Alibaba and Ant.

00:01:44.647 --> 00:01:46.620
(dramatic music)

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:48.670
It all started with this speech by Jack Ma

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.287
in October of last year.

00:01:50.287 --> 00:01:53.130
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.170
- [Quentin] In this speech,
Jack Ma effectively criticized

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.830
the people responsible for
overseeing the Chinese economy

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.282
and for overseeing his companies.

00:02:02.282 --> 00:02:06.199
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.237
- And as The Wall Street
Journal has reported,

00:02:11.237 --> 00:02:14.480
that infuriated China's to leaders

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.242
and in fact, President Xi Jinping himself

00:02:17.242 --> 00:02:18.810
made the decision,

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.210
my colleagues have reported,

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.400
to scupper the pending IPO of Ant

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.350
as a result partly of the speech.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.980
- Ant was supposed to list
on Thursday and not anymore.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.628
- [Narrator] What would have
been the world's largest IPO

00:02:32.628 --> 00:02:35.790
was called off less than
two weeks after that speech.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.970
- That kind of direct intervention

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.890
by a national-level leader

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.630
in what is effectively
a commercial process,

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.150
it's not like you would necessarily

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.550
see something equivalent happening

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.880
in the US.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:49.880
- [Narrator] About two months later,

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.396
Chinese regulators came down
hard on Ma's two companies.

00:02:53.396 --> 00:02:55.240
They criticized Ant's behavior

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.940
toward consumers and rivals

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.330
and told it to refocus
on it payments business

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:01.530
and fix problems in newer ventures.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.270
Regulators also launched
an antitrust investigation

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.670
into Alibaba, saying the company abused

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.280
its dominant market position,

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.520
forcing some sellers to
operate only on its platforms.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:13.645
Alibaba didn't comment on the allegations,

00:03:13.645 --> 00:03:16.940
while Ant said it
appreciated the guidance.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:18.990
That probe lasted less than four months

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:23.200
and Alibaba was hit with a
$2.8 billion antitrust fine

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.270
while Ant will soon be directly overseen

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.920
by China's central bank.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.010
So for Ma's speech to penalties,

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.220
regulators made it all
happen in under six months.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.240
- [Quentin] In the US, you might
expect some of these things

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:36.040
to last many years.

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:36.873
- [Narrator] Just take a look

00:03:36.873 --> 00:03:38.420
at four American big tech giants

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.660
that have been accused of
anti-competitive behavior

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.160
in the digital marketplace.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.370
- The testimony you are about give

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:45.840
is true and correct to the
best of your knowledge,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.390
information and belief, so help you God.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.730
- [Narrator] While the usually
visible Jack Ma disappeared

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.470
after the IPO was scrapped,

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:55.660
in the US, the CEOs were
called to a very public hearing

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.198
in front of House lawmakers.

00:03:57.198 --> 00:03:58.210
- [Quentin] You had four

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.920
of the most powerful technology executives

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.510
in the world subject to
hours of hostile questioning,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.530
which came from both sides of the aisle.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:07.363
- [Narrator] This hearing came

00:04:07.363 --> 00:04:09.870
amid a Congressional fact
finding investigation

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.150
that had been underway
for more than a year.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.980
Remember, Chinese regulators'
antitrust investigation

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.240
into Alibaba from start to
finish took about four months.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:22.100
At the end of the House
Democrats' 16-month probe,

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.070
lawmakers concluded
that the four companies

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.300
had leveraged their dominance

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:28.480
to stamp out competition
and stifle innovation.

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.990
Republicans said they supported

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.130
strong antitrust enforcement
targeting the companies.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:35.640
The four companies disputed the findings.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.200
Since then, there have been a series

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.690
of blockbuster lawsuits launched

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.460
by US federal agencies and
state governments aimed

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.040
at enforcing existing antitrust rules

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.350
but as of April, US regulators

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.430
and lawmakers haven't
ordered these companies

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.620
to reform their business practices.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.040
- The US is, of course, a democracy

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.711
with all of the check and balances

00:04:53.711 --> 00:04:56.280
and requirements for transparency

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.750
that that involves.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.100
And that means that
companies can push back.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.010
- [Narrator] For example,
the popular Chinese-owned

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.640
video sharing app TikTok.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.920
- We're looking at TikTok,

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.700
we may be banning TikTok.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.870
In August last year,

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.210
the Trump administration
signed an executive order

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.500
that could effectively
ban Americans from using

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:13.840
and downloading the app.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.630
This was over concerns that user data

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:17.810
could be shared with
the Chinese government.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.500
TikTok said that the Chinese government

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.310
has never asked for user data

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.360
and will refuse such a request.

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:27.040
Within the US legal system,
the company fought back.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.570
TikTok filed lawsuits against the order

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:30.210
and less than two months later,

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:33.000
a federal judge blocked
the administration's ban.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.810
But for Jack Ma and his companies,

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:36.610
there was no room for appeal.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:37.820
- Chinese political context,

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.550
basically it makes it much harder

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.500
for companies or others to push back

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.950
if they disagree.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.060
- [Narrator] Alibaba
immediately accepted the fine

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.480
and said it would invest in measures

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.720
to support merchants on its platforms,

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.810
while Ant said it would
maintain the continuity

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:53.400
and quality of its services

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.492
while it fully complies with regulations.

00:05:55.492 --> 00:05:57.220
This regulatory assault

00:05:57.220 --> 00:05:59.910
has also gone beyond Jack Ma's companies.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.050
A few days later,

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:03.730
nearly three dozen other
big tech companies in China

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:05.060
also vowed to comply

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.940
with the country's
anti-monopoly regulations.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.440
So while these two companies
have been shining examples

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.990
of Chinese innovation,

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.660
from Beijing's perspective,

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.040
their success needs to align

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.100
with the party's interests.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:17.933
- If there was a sense

00:06:17.933 --> 00:06:19.850
in which it was allowing
the private sector

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:22.446
to command bits of the economy,

00:06:22.446 --> 00:06:25.770
it is now pushing Alibaba
and other companies

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.830
to fall more tightly in line

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.800
with its own priorities.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:34.070
It's about making sure
that government control

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.223
or party control over the
Chinese economy is secure.

